// A call argument the JSON parser cannot deserialize keeps its position.  The
// Ghidra serializer writes `"kind": "unknown"` for a varnode it cannot
// classify; the parser used to skip such an input, which moved every later
// argument one parameter to the left before the lifter saw the call.
//
//   ext_fixed(a, <unknown>, b)   declared (int, int, int): was ext_fixed(a, b, 0U)
//   ext_var(a, <unknown>, b)     declared (int, ...):      was ext_var(a, b), with
//                                no diagnostic even under -strict
//   ext_obj(a, 7, b)             the middle input is not a JSON object
//
// Each call is now dropped and reported, a warning by default and an error
// under -strict.
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -print-tu -output %t > %t.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=WARN %s --input-file %t.log
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=C %s --input-file %t.c
// RUN: test -e %t.cir
// RUN: not %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -strict -output %t.strict > %t.strict.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=ERR %s --input-file %t.strict.log
// RUN: test ! -e %t.strict.cir
//
